WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.400
LG was the third largest phone maker in the world.
They were selling around 120 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.360
phones a year.
But, in 2021&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:18.880
after 23 consecutive quarters of no profit, and&nbsp;
losing $4.5 billion, LG left mobile altogether.&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.600
A year after they had proudly said "LG's mobile&nbsp;
business is going to be profitable by 2021".&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:34.640
LG is the strangest phone company in the entire&nbsp;
industry, because despite these losses, it might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.840
also be the most important phone company.
So many crucial parts of your current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.200
phone were first pioneered by LG.
The two rear cameras, quad-core,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:52.000
ultra-wide camera — all were first done by LG.&nbsp;
Even a modular phone, an extendable screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.840
and a "T" shaped phone.
They even had a no-stylus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.600
touchscreen before Apple.
LG was the most innovative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.600
smartphone company, by far.
So why did it fail so badly?&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:18.320
Well, as it turns out, LG kept making&nbsp;
the same three mistakes over and over.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.680
The crazy part about all this is how&nbsp;
popular LG phones were back in the day.&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:31.440
In the 2000s, LG was actually dominating, and&nbsp;
their phones were really popular and… really good?

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.400
I bet there are a bunch of you&nbsp;
watching whose first or second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:40.960
phone was the Voyager or the LG Chocolate.
These were pretty awesome, and back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:47.120
LG was making a lot of breakthroughs.
In 2006, LG announced the Prada. The first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:53.360
capacitive touchscreen smartphone, no stylus&nbsp;
required. Months before the iPhone reveal.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.184
In fact, LG actually believed Apple&nbsp;
stole the idea from the Prada.&nbsp;

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.000
[Woo-Young Kwak, head of LG Mobile Handset&nbsp;
R&amp;D Centre]: "We consider that Apple copied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.280
the Prada phone after the design was unveiled&nbsp;
when it was presented in the iF Design Award&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:11.520
and won the prize in September 2006."
But this is just the tip of the iceberg.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:17.680
The LG Optimus 2X, the first dual-core&nbsp;
phone, and the first to have 1080p video.&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.840
The Optimus 3D, the first&nbsp;
to have two rear cameras.&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:29.040
The Optimus 4X, the first quad-core phone.
The first QHD display with the LG G3.&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.040
The G5 with the first ultra-wide camera.
The V40, the first with three rear cameras.&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.360
And there are even more than I mentioned here.
LG was on a roll, and many of these became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.440
standard in all other major phone brands.
By 2008, LG was the third-largest mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.720
phone manufacturer in the world.
They were selling around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:57.040
120 million phones a year.
Then came the G series, their most popular phone.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.240
But pretty quickly, LG phones&nbsp;
were selling worse and worse.&nbsp;

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.200
Why?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.880
Well, with how groundbreaking a lot of LG&nbsp;
phones were, they came with some drawbacks.&nbsp;

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.080
LG was hardware-first, which was&nbsp;
the first of LG's big mistakes.&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.600
Groundbreaking, trendsetting.
New technology often comes with drawbacks.&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:25.760
For one, not all ideas were a hit.
The LG Optimus 3D was also the world's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.920
first mobile with a glasses-free 3D display.
Not as influential as the two rear cameras.&nbsp;

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.400
Or the LG G Flex — a curved&nbsp;
screen, and a self-healing back.&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.760
The G4 had a leather back and a curved display.
But it suffered from a boot loop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.640
which made it unusable.
The G5 was a modular smartphone.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:11.200
Cool idea! But they abandoned it soon after.
There was also the G8 ThinQ, which had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.520
hand recognition sensor, so you could&nbsp;
control your phone without touching it!&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.120
Which uh, didn't really work most of the time.&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.600
They quickly abandoned that too.
You can probably see the problem.&nbsp;

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:30.320
LG was getting a bit carried away with new ideas.
Even if LG was first most of the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.520
why would you buy into a new cool idea when&nbsp;
so many of them were killed right away?

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:42.480
Also, because of all the new features and&nbsp;
ideas, these phones cost far more due to R&amp;D.&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:49.200
Q3 2016 had a mobile loss of&nbsp;
$389.4M, with revenue down 23%.&nbsp;

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.240
Despite selling 55 million phones.
For context, Samsung at this time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:05:00.000
recorded its best quarter in years.
If not for mobile, LG's overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.840
operating profit that quarter would have&nbsp;
been $650 million instead of $252 million.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:12.720
The phone business was destroying the company.
After the 2000s, LG's market share had collapsed.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.280
And it wasn't just them.
Sony had basically disappeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.520
same with Nokia and Blackberry.
They shipped around 56 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:28.320
phones in 2017, then 39 million in&nbsp;
2018, and then 33 million in 2019.&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:33.520
LG needed to change, and drastically.
Either drop mobile, or dramatically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.480
improve profits.
The latter would be a big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:46.480
challenge — and would it even be worth it?
Well, one man arrived determined to try.

